content.text:
Set the static `options` property on your Agent class to `{ hibernate: false }`:

```ts
import { Agent } from "agents";

export class AlwaysOnAgent extends Agent {
  static options = { hibernate: false };
}
```

This comes from the Cloudflare Agents WebSocket API reference. Hibernation is on by default. With it on, the agent can be evicted from memory while WebSocket connections are idle and woken again when a message arrives.

If you turn it off, the Durable Object stays in memory for as long as connections are open. In-memory state will persist between messages, but you'll pay for the whole time the connection is open, not just the time spent handling messages.

Ludion had no lessons on this, so the answer is from the official docs.

Sources:
- [Cloudflare Agents – WebSockets API reference](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/api-reference/websockets/)
- [cloudflare/agents docs (GitHub)](https://github.com/cloudflare/agents/tree/main/docs)

